title: 'fungible: allow deposits below ED into accounts with funds on hold'
doc:
- audience:
  - Runtime Dev
  - Runtime User
  description: |-
    Fixes #9903.

    Pool members can stake their whole balance, ED included. Delegated staking puts all of it on hold and gives the account an extra provider, so the account stays alive with no free balance. pallet-balances is fine with that. It only dusts an account when free is below ED and nothing is held.

    The deposit side didn't agree. The default `fungible::Unbalanced::increase_balance` and `pallet-balances::can_deposit` only looked at the free balance, so any deposit that left it below ED was treated as going into a new account. With `BestEffort` the deposit returned `Ok(0)` and nothing landed. That's how staking pays rewards, so small rewards just vanished. With `Exact` or a transfer it failed with `BelowMinimum`, which meant a member with a pending reward below ED couldn't `claim_payout`, and couldn't `unbond` either, because unbond pays out rewards first. They were stuck until the reward grew past ED.

    Now an account is only treated as new when its total balance is zero, which is what the doc comment on `increase_balance` already said.

    cc @Ank4n @muharem @ggwpez
crates:
- name: pallet-balances
  bump: minor
- name: frame-support
  bump: minor
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
